## HOW TO START THE NEW PLATFORM BUILD

1. Research the platform's current algorithm/discovery mechanics, current 
   best-performing formats, current safe posting frequency, and any recent 
   platform changes — don't assume anything is still true from training data.
2. Ask Gaurav for the content source/hub he wants to drive traffic to (same 
   as the Pinterest content-hub audit) — don't assume it's the same website 
   unless confirmed.
3. Propose a small number of focus content clusters/categories based on 
   content depth, same way Pinterest's evergreen boards were chosen — don't 
   spread thin across everything.
4. Test the platform's actual generative/creative unit (whatever the 
   equivalent of "one pin" is — one Reel script, one carousel, one video 
   concept) on a single real example before building the full daily system.
5. Only after the above is proven, build the fixed daily schedule, the 
   deterministic rotation mechanisms, the output format, and the plain- 
   language usage guide — in that order.
6. Confirm ambiguous instructions back to Gaurav before building on them, 
   especially anything involving volume, counts, or "how many/how often."
7. Verify any generated data file (link lists, schedules, rotations) 
   programmatically for gaps/duplicates/correct sequencing before presenting 
   it as final.

